Text:
fearlessManager is a program that attempts to become the 'single' manager.
The 'single' manager applies the messages that fearlessMessage sends, one at a time.
The 'manager path' is the path of the ManagerFolder (see the Implementation notes).
projects.info is a file containing an Info serialized as defined in the fearless standard library.
We expect that only the manager can edit this file.
The Info of projects.info is a ProjectsInfo.

Grammar:
ManagerFolder ::= LockFile, "projects.info", "icons", "locks"
//icons and locks are folders.
LockFile ::= "no_manager.lock" | "candidate_manager.lock" | "single_manager_at_", Port, ".lock" //the digits are a port of the loopback address
Port ::= [1-9][0-9]*
ProjectsInfo ::= Infos.map("projects", Projects, "reserve", Extensions)
Projects ::= Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn)
Extensions ::= Infos.list(Extension1 .. Extensionn) //1..n can be empty
TypeNames ::= Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen)
Project ::= Infos.map("path", TaggedText, "kind", Kind, "mains", TypeNames, "mounts", Mount, "attenuators", Attenuator)
Mount ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, ProjectName1 .. TypeNamen, ProjectNamen)
Attenuator ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, TypeNames1 .. TypeNamen, TypeNamesn)
Kind ::= "idle" | "code" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
Extension ::= OSExtension
ProjectName ::= ValidSegment
TaggedText ::= double quote, [Str:|UStr:|Base16:], [0-9A-Za-z_.....]
ProgressLine ::= at most 80 characters saying what fearlessManager is doing and how much of it is done, with no time in it, as "Ending the mains: 2 of 5 ended."

Well formedness:
in Port: the digits form a number smaller than 65536.
in Extension: not in 'fearless' or 'ffile000'-'ffile999' or 'fapp000'-'fapp999'.
in Projects: no two Project with equal TaggedText.
in Extensions: all Extension are disjoint.
in Project: all TypeName in TypeNames are disjoint.
in TaggedText: second component is 'Str:' if the third component is the result of p.escape where p is a Fearless Str encoding a valid OS FS path.
in TaggedText: second component is 'UStr:' if the third component is the result of p.escape where p is a Fearless UStr encoding a valid OS FS path.
in TaggedText: second component is 'Base16:' if the third component is [0-9A-F]* and is a valid OS FS path when decoded.

Invariant:
At every moment, at most one fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.

Define fearlessManager:
A No folder is at the 'manager path'.
B fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder: no_manager.lock, projects.info holding Infos.map("projects", Infos.list(), "reserve", Infos.list()), and the empty folders icons and locks.
C fearlessManager takes the lock of no_manager.lock.
D fearlessManager.serve()

Define fearlessManager:
A No folder is at the 'manager path'.
B Another process creates a folder at the 'manager path' before fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder.
C fearlessManager ends.

Define fearlessManager:
A The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile, no_manager.lock, and no process holds the lock of no_manager.lock.
B fearlessManager takes the lock of no_manager.lock.
C fearlessManager.serve()

Define fearlessManager:
A The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile, candidate_manager.lock or single_manager_at_X.lock, and no process holds the lock of that LockFile.
B fearlessManager takes the lock of that LockFile.
C fearlessManager renames that LockFile to no_manager.lock.
D fearlessManager.serve()

Define fearlessManager:
A Another process holds the lock of the LockFile of the folder at the 'manager path'.
B fearlessManager ends.

Define fearlessManager:
A The folder at the 'manager path' holds no LockFile, or more than one LockFile.
B fearlessManager.fatalError(an error naming the 'manager path', and saying that the folder there is not a ManagerFolder)

Define fearlessManager.serve():
A fearlessManager holds the lock of no_manager.lock, and the folder at the 'manager path' is a ManagerFolder.
B fearlessManager renames no_manager.lock to candidate_manager.lock.
C fearlessManager copies base.IconsConflict and base.IconsFearless into icons.
D For each Project p of projects.info with the Kind code: Coordinator.dropUnfinished(p).
E fearlessManager.buildMap()
F fearlessManager listens for connections on the loopback address, on a port X that the OS picks.
G fearlessManager renames candidate_manager.lock to single_manager_at_X.lock.
H fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.
I fearlessManager shows its tray icon.
J For each message m, one at a time, in the order the messages arrive: fearlessManager.receive(m).

Define fearlessManager.serve():
A fearlessManager holds the lock of no_manager.lock, and the folder at the 'manager path' is not a ManagerFolder.
B fearlessManager.fatalError(an error naming the 'manager path', and saying that the folder there is not a ManagerFolder)

Define fearlessManager.receive(m):
A fearlessManager.nameInference()
B fearlessManager.autoCheck(p), when m is about the registered project p.
C fearlessManager.apply(m)

Define fearlessManager.accept(m):
A fearlessManager sends Applied on the connection of m.
B When the manager GUI is running, fearlessManager tells the manager GUI that m is Applied.
C fearlessManager sends on the connection of m what m writes in the Output, until m ends writing.
D fearlessManager ends the connection of m.

Define fearlessManager.refuse(m, e):
A fearlessManager sends Refused and e on the connection of m.
B When the manager GUI is running, fearlessManager tells the manager GUI that m is Refused.
C fearlessManager ends the connection of m.

Define fearlessManager.apply(Show):
A No manager GUI is running.
B ManagerGui.start
C fearlessManager.accept(Show)

Define fearlessManager.apply(Show):
A The manager GUI is running.
B fearlessManager.accept(Show)

Define fearlessManager.apply(Quit):
A fearlessManager sends Applied on the connection of Quit.
B fearlessManager sends a ProgressLine on the connection of Quit every 2 seconds, until fearlessManager ends.
C Every message m that arrives until fearlessManager ends: fearlessManager.refuse(m, an error naming the verb of m and the end of the 'single' manager).
D For each p in busyProjects: fearlessManager.terminate(p).
E fearlessManager renames its LockFile to no_manager.lock.
F fearlessManager ends.

Define fearlessManager.apply(Reset):
A fearlessManager sends Applied on the connection of Reset.
B fearlessManager.reset()

Define fearlessManager.fatalError(e):
A fearlessManager shows a dialog with e and the names of the busyProjects.
B The user closes the dialog.
C fearlessManager.reset()

Define fearlessManager.reset():
A Every message m that arrives until fearlessManager ends: fearlessManager.refuse(m, an error naming the verb of m and the end of the 'single' manager).
B For each p in busyProjects: fearlessManager.terminate(p).
C Reconciliator.eradicateAll
D fearlessManager deletes the folder at the 'manager path'.
E fearlessManager ends.

Implementation notes:
The 'manager path' is the folder fearless<version> next to the program folder, the folder holding fearlessManager, fearlessMessage and fearlessOnClick.
fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder by filling a new folder next to the 'manager path', then renaming that new folder to the 'manager path': the rename fails when a folder is at the 'manager path' already.
The lock of a LockFile is the lock of FileChannel.tryLock: the OS releases the lock when the process ends, however the process ends, and the lock follows the file when the file is renamed.
